---
/*
 * Notifications, the macOS menu bar panel and gnosis:// links. The panel capture is a 360 pt popover, so it sits
 * under a plain menu bar strip with the app's real tray icon instead of inside a full window frame.
 */
---

<section class="needs-you frame" id="needs-you" aria-labelledby="needs-you-title">
  <div class="needs-you-copy">
    <h2 id="needs-you-title">Know when a PR needs you</h2>
    <p class="needs-you-lead">
      Gnosis watches your review requests and your own PRs while it runs. When one needs you, it tells you once and
      opens the PR at the right tab.
    </p>
    <dl class="needs-you-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Notifications</dt>
        <dd>
          On the desktop when Gnosis is in the background, in the app when it isn’t. One per event: review requested,
          approved, changes requested, checks failed, ready to merge, and explanation ready. A notification never writes
          to GitHub.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>
          Menu bar panel <span>macOS</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Click the Gnosis icon to see what needs you, grouped as To review, To fix, and Ready. Open a PR with a click,
          or with the arrow keys and Return. The number on the icon and the Dock counts new PRs that need you.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Open in Gnosis</dt>
        <dd>
          <code>gnosis://</code> links open a PR in Gnosis at a chosen tab. Use Copy Gnosis link in a PR’s actions to
          share one. An Open in Gnosis extension for Chrome, Edge, and Firefox adds a button to GitHub PR pages. It is
          coming to the browser stores.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <figure class="menubar-shot">
    <div class="menubar-scene">
      <div class="menubar-strip" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="menubar-item">
          <img src="/menubar-icon.png" alt="" width="22" height="22" />
          <span>4</span>
        </span>
      </div>
      <img
        class="menubar-panel"
        src="/screenshots/menubar-panel.webp"
        srcset="/screenshots/menubar-panel-small.webp 360w, /screenshots/menubar-panel.webp 720w"
        sizes="360px"
        alt="The Gnosis menu bar panel: 6 need you, 4 new, 1 ready. PRs are grouped as To review, including a three-PR stack, To fix, with changes requested and merge conflicts, and Ready."
        width="360"
        height="534"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      The menu bar panel, opened from the Gnosis icon.
      <span>Actual app · sample repository</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
